	'project_delivery_foundations_h3' => 'Your instructor',
	'project_delivery_foundations_b3' => 'Tomasz Wierzbicki is the project-management lead instructor. He teaches this course and Advanced Project Leadership, course 03. You hear him in the recordings. He does not sit in a room with you, because the academy is fully online. Questions about a lesson can go to learner support at support@shikaku-academy.example during support hours, Monday to Friday from 08:00 to 18:00 CET and Saturday from 09:00 to 13:00 CET. Priya Raman leads that desk. Live Q&A, if you bought this course on its own, is monthly, on a Wednesday at 19:00 CET. If this course is part of a pathway bundle or of all-access, live Q&A is weekly at that same time, and Tomasz\'s feedback on two assignments is included. On a single-course purchase, that feedback is not included. The certificate you download is still a certificate of completion either way.',
	'lesson_player_title' => 'Lesson player',
	'lesson_player_intro' => 'Purchased lessons open in the lesson player, in a numbered list, at your pace. The mock exam and the certificate of completion come after the lessons, not before them.',
	'lesson_player_h1' => 'The lesson and the list',
	'lesson_player_b1' => 'After you pay, the course appears in My courses. Open it and the lesson plays as video, with the rest of the course in a numbered list. Project Delivery Foundations lists 24 lessons that together run 18 hours. Agile Practitioner Track lists 20 lessons and 15 hours. Advanced Project Leadership lists 32 lessons and 26 hours. The IT courses use the same player: Cloud Fundamentals is 22 lessons and 16 hours, IT Service Management Essentials is 26 lessons and 20 hours, and Network & Security Basics is 28 lessons and 22 hours. You choose the lesson by its place in that list, watch, and come back later during your access period. Nothing in the player asks you to be online at a fixed class time. Live Q&A is separate. It is held on Wednesdays at 19:00 CET, monthly or weekly according to your plan. The player itself is only for the recorded lesson.',
	'lesson_player_h2' => 'Progress, the mock exam, and the certificate',
	'lesson_player_b2' => 'A progress marker shows how far you have moved through the lesson list. It is a position in the course, so you can see what you have already opened. Study at your pace inside the access you paid for: 12 months on a single course, 18 months on a pathway bundle, or 24 months on all-access. A study planner is included on every plan and simply shows the lessons ahead. When you have worked through the list, take the mock exam. A single course includes one mock exam. A pathway bundle includes the mock exam for each course in that track. All-access includes the mock exam for all six courses. After the mock exam, download your certificate of completion. That document is Shikaku Academy\'s record that you finished the course. It is not an external credential, and the academy does not publish a pass rate for the mock exam or for any outside exam.',
	'plans_title' => 'Plans and pricing',
