	'in_n1' => 'Helena Marsh',
	'in_r1' => 'Founder and director of studies',
	'in_b1' => 'Helena Marsh founded Shikaku Academy in 2017 and is director of studies. She sets the standard for the six courses and for the lessons recorded at Kade 14, 3072 Rotterdam, Netherlands. She does not teach a numbered course. Tomasz Wierzbicki, Amara Osei, Rafael Quintero, Ingrid Solberg, and Daniel Mwangi record the courses. Priya Raman leads learner support. With Helena, that is a team of seven. Her work is the outline before a lesson is recorded, the line between the project-management pathway and the IT pathway, and the decision to publish a certificate of completion rather than a claim about an outside exam. The academy is fully online. Learners do not come to Rotterdam for class. The studio is where the lessons are made and where the support desk is based. She asks the site to stay specific: a lesson count, an hour count, a price, and an access period. No pass rate is published.',
	'in_n2' => 'Tomasz Wierzbicki',
	'in_r2' => 'Project-management lead',
	'in_b2' => 'Tomasz Wierzbicki is the project-management lead instructor. He teaches course 01, Project Delivery Foundations, and course 03, Advanced Project Leadership. Course 01 is 24 lessons and 18 hours, priced at $149. Course 03 is 32 lessons and 26 hours, priced at $229. His lessons stay inside the work of delivery: framing a piece of work, planning it, keeping status visible, and closing it. On a single course he is the instructor in the recordings. You take one mock exam and you may download a certificate of completion. Instructor feedback on two assignments is included when his course sits inside a pathway bundle or all-access. It is not included on a single course. The project-management bundle, which also holds Amara Osei\'s course, is $429 for 18 months. He does not publish a pass rate for any external credential. The courses prepare you for widely recognised project-management credentials. The certificate is the academy\'s own.',
	'in_n3' => 'Amara Osei',
	'in_r3' => 'Agile',
	'in_b3' => 'Amara Osei teaches course 02, Agile Practitioner Track: 20 lessons, 15 hours, priced at $169. It is the agile course on the project-management pathway, between Project Delivery Foundations and Advanced Project Leadership. Her lessons treat agile as a way a working team can show the work, keep a short cycle, and decide what should happen next. She records the course for the lesson player, so you can pause and return during your access period. If you bought only this course, you have 12 months of access, one mock exam, live Q&A monthly, a study planner, and a certificate of completion. Feedback on two assignments is not part of that single purchase. If course 02 is inside the pathway bundle or all-access, that feedback is included. The bundle price is $429 for the three project-management courses. Live Q&A, at the frequency your plan allows, is on Wednesdays at 19:00 CET. No student story on this site is tied only to her course.',
	'in_n4' => 'Rafael Quintero',
	'in_r4' => 'Cloud',
	'in_b4' => 'Rafael Quintero teaches course 04, Cloud Fundamentals, on the IT pathway: 22 lessons, 16 hours, priced at $159. The course is an introduction to cloud ideas for people who want a steady sequence rather than a tour of a named platform. He does not teach a vendor product, and the lessons do not carry a brand. You watch them in the lesson player and, on a single purchase, take one mock exam. That purchase includes 12 months of access, live Q&A monthly, a study planner, and a certificate of completion. Noor Haddad, whose story moves from returning to work to cloud support associate, took this course. Inside the IT pathway bundle, course 04 sits with courses 05 and 06 for $429 and 18 months. All-access includes it, with the project-management courses, for $690 and 24 months. Weekly live Q&A on those two plans is on Wednesdays at 19:00 CET. Feedback on two assignments follows the same plan rule.',
	'in_n5' => 'Ingrid Solberg',
	'in_r5' => 'Service management',
