	'in_n6' => 'Daniel Mwangi',
	'in_r6' => 'Network and security',
	'in_b6' => 'Daniel Mwangi teaches course 06, Network & Security Basics: 28 lessons, 22 hours, priced at $189. It is the last course on the IT pathway. The lessons cover the basics of networks and security as an academy course, without a named product and without a named certification. You study in the lesson player at your own pace. One mock exam closes the course on a single purchase, and the certificate of completion is available after that exam. Access on a single purchase lasts 12 months, with live Q&A monthly. If you take the IT pathway bundle, this course is one of the three, with Cloud Fundamentals and IT Service Management Essentials, at $429 for 18 months. All-access includes it for 24 months at $690. Weekly live Q&A on that bundle, and on all-access, is on Wednesdays at 19:00 CET. Feedback on two assignments is included on those plans and is not included on a single course. Questions that cannot wait go to learner support.',
	'in_n7' => 'Priya Raman',
	'in_r7' => 'Learner support lead',
	'in_b7' => 'Priya Raman is learner support lead. She does not teach one of the six courses. She answers support@shikaku-academy.example during the published hours: Monday to Friday, 08:00 to 18:00 CET, and Saturday, 09:00 to 13:00 CET. Write with the course name, the lesson\'s place in the list if you have it, and what you already tried. She routes a teaching question to the instructor for that course: Tomasz Wierzbicki for courses 01 and 03, Amara Osei for course 02, Rafael Quintero for course 04, Ingrid Solberg for course 05, or Daniel Mwangi for course 06. Live Q&A remains on Wednesdays at 19:00 CET and follows your plan, monthly or weekly. Refund questions use the same desk. A refund is available within 14 days if you have watched less than 20 percent, on every plan. The support office is at Kade 14, 3072 Rotterdam, Netherlands, in the same place as the recording studio. You do not need to visit in order to study or to be answered.',
	'student_stories_title' => 'Student stories',
	'student_stories_intro' => 'Three learners name the role they left and the role they hold, and the course or bundle they took. These accounts are not pass rates and they are not salaries.',
	'student_stories_h1' => 'Lucía Ferrer, operations coordinator to project coordinator',
	'student_stories_b1' => 'Lucía Ferrer was an operations coordinator. She is now a project coordinator. She took the project-management pathway bundle: Project Delivery Foundations, Agile Practitioner Track, and Advanced Project Leadership. The bundle is $429 and includes 18 months of access, a mock exam for each of the three courses, live Q&A weekly, a study planner, a certificate of completion, and instructor feedback on two assignments. Tomasz Wierzbicki teaches courses 01 and 03. Amara Osei teaches course 02. Together the recordings run 18 hours, 15 hours, and 26 hours.

"I wanted the language of a delivery: how to frame the work, how to keep it visible, and how to stay with it once other people depended on the plan. The three courses are that sequence, in order, at a pace I could keep."

She studied in the lesson player during those 18 months and downloaded a certificate of completion for each course she finished. The role change is the account she gives. It is not a pass rate, and it is not a salary. The academy does not treat her story as a promise to the next buyer.',
	'student_stories_h2' => 'Jonas Becker, help-desk analyst to service desk lead',
	'student_stories_b2' => 'Jonas Becker was a help-desk analyst. He is now a service desk lead. He took course 05, IT Service Management Essentials, taught by Ingrid Solberg. The course is 26 lessons and 20 hours, priced at $179. Bought on its own, it includes 12 months of access, one mock exam, live Q&A monthly, a study planner, and a certificate of completion. It does not include instructor feedback on two assignments. That feedback belongs to the pathway bundle and to all-access.

"The queue was already my work. What I needed was language for the service, for who takes a request next, and for which request should go first. I could replay a lesson when I had not been able to hold the idea the first time."

He took the mock exam and downloaded his certificate of completion from Shikaku Academy. The course prepares people for widely recognised IT credentials. It did not award one to him, and the academy does not say that the new role was a result it can repeat. His account stops at the role he names and the course he took.',
	'student_stories_h3' => 'Noor Haddad, returning to work to cloud support associate',
	'student_stories_b3' => 'Noor Haddad was returning to work. She is now a cloud support associate. She took course 04, Cloud Fundamentals, taught by Rafael Quintero. The course is 22 lessons and 16 hours, priced at $159. On a single course she had 12 months of access, one mock exam, live Q&A monthly on Wednesdays at 19:00 CET, a study planner, and a certificate of completion.

"I had been away from a desk. I needed lessons I could stop and start, not a room I had to reach at a fixed hour. I watched the course in order, then used the mock exam to see what I could explain in my own words."

She used the study planner and wrote to learner support when a lesson needed a plainer explanation. Support is open Monday to Friday from 08:00 to 18:00 CET and Saturday from 09:00 to 13:00 CET, at support@shikaku-academy.example. She downloaded a certificate of completion. The course prepared her for widely recognised IT credentials. It did not confer one, and it did not come with a salary figure. The story is this change of role, and this course.',
	'about_title' => 'About',
