	'about_h1' => 'Helena Marsh',
	'about_b1' => 'I founded Shikaku Academy in 2017. I am director of studies, and I do not teach one of the six numbered courses. I wanted preparation for a credential to be quiet enough to sit beside a job: recorded lessons, a pace you set, and a certificate that says only what it is. The lessons are made at our studio, then left in the lesson player. You begin after you pay. You do not wait for a room to fill, and you do not travel here for class. My work is the outline before a lesson is recorded, the line between the project-management pathway and the IT pathway, and the refusal to borrow the name of an outside credential. We prepare you for widely recognised project-management and IT credentials. We do not award them. I would rather publish a lesson count, an hour count, and a price than a promise about an exam we do not control. The site does not carry a pass rate, because I will not invent one.',
	'about_h2' => 'The office, the team, and the limits',
	'about_b2' => 'The recording studio and the support office are at Kade 14, 3072 Rotterdam, Netherlands. That is our address. It is not a campus, and there is no visit day. We are a team of seven. I direct studies. Tomasz Wierzbicki teaches Project Delivery Foundations and Advanced Project Leadership. Amara Osei teaches Agile Practitioner Track. Rafael Quintero teaches Cloud Fundamentals. Ingrid Solberg teaches IT Service Management Essentials. Daniel Mwangi teaches Network & Security Basics. Priya Raman leads learner support. Support is open Monday to Friday from 08:00 to 18:00 CET and Saturday from 09:00 to 13:00 CET, at support@shikaku-academy.example. Live Q&A is on Wednesdays at 19:00 CET. Prices are in USD. A single course starts at $149 for 12 months, a pathway bundle is $429 for 18 months, and all-access is $690 for 24 months. The certificate we issue is a certificate of completion. If a sentence on this site cannot be checked against those facts, it does not belong here.',
