	'support_h1' => 'Support hours',
	'support_b1' => 'Learner support is open Monday to Friday from 08:00 to 18:00 CET, and Saturday from 09:00 to 13:00 CET. The email is support@shikaku-academy.example. Priya Raman leads the desk. She does not teach a numbered course. She answers questions about access, payment, refunds, and where a lesson sits in the player, and she routes a teaching question to the right instructor. Tomasz Wierzbicki takes courses 01 and 03, Amara Osei takes course 02, Rafael Quintero takes course 04, Ingrid Solberg takes course 05, and Daniel Mwangi takes course 06. Use the form on this page or write to the email. Name the course, and the lesson\'s place in the list if you have reached one. If you have not bought yet, say which course or plan you are considering. The prices you should be quoted are the published ones: a single course from $149, a pathway bundle at $429, or all-access at $690, in USD, with VAT shown at checkout.',
	'support_h2' => 'Live Q&A on Wednesdays',
	'support_b2' => 'Live Q&A is on Wednesdays at 19:00 CET. It is not the same thing as the support desk. The desk answers during the Monday to Saturday hours above. Q&A is a set time for course questions. How often you may join depends on the plan. A single course includes live Q&A monthly. A pathway bundle includes it weekly. All-access includes it weekly. The session does not replace the recorded lessons, and it is not a second course. You can continue in the lesson player whether or not you join. Bring something you have already watched. If you are blocked before Wednesday, write to support@shikaku-academy.example and Priya will send a teaching question to the instructor of that course. Refunds are not decided on the Q&A call. A refund request belongs with the desk, and it follows one rule on every plan: within 14 days, if you have watched less than 20 percent.',
	'support_h3' => 'The Rotterdam office',
	'support_b3' => 'The recording studio and the support office are at Kade 14, 3072 Rotterdam, Netherlands. Shikaku Academy was founded in 2017 and is fully online, so this address is where lessons are recorded and where support is based. It is not a classroom you need to visit, and you can finish a course without coming to Rotterdam. The team of seven works from here: Helena Marsh, director of studies; the five instructors named on the courses; and Priya Raman on learner support. A message sent through the form on this page reaches the same desk as an email to support@shikaku-academy.example. Write during the published hours if you want a reply inside those hours. Say whether your note is about a course you have bought, a plan you have not yet bought, or a receipt. Have the course name ready. We will answer from the facts already published: lessons, hours, price, access, and the certificate of completion.',
	'faq_title' => 'FAQ',
	'faq_intro' => 'Twelve answers are grouped under Buying, Learning, Access, and Certificates. The figures here are the same ones used on Plans and pricing.',
	'faq_q1' => 'Can I buy a single course?',
	'faq_g1' => 'Buying',
	'faq_a1' => 'Yes. A single course is one title from the six, with access for 12 months. Project Delivery Foundations is $149, Agile Practitioner Track is $169, Advanced Project Leadership is $229, Cloud Fundamentals is $159, IT Service Management Essentials is $179, and Network & Security Basics is $189. The plan line "from $149" is the lowest of those prices, not a discount on the others. You receive one mock exam, live Q&A monthly, a study planner, and a certificate of completion. You do not receive instructor feedback on two assignments. You pay by card at checkout, in USD, with VAT shown there. After payment the course appears in My courses and opens in the lesson player. If you later want the rest of a pathway, this page does not list an upgrade price. It lists the bundle and all-access as separate plans, at $429 and $690.',
	'faq_q2' => 'What is included in the pathway bundle?',
	'faq_g2' => 'Buying',
	'faq_a2' => 'The pathway bundle costs $429 and includes three courses of one track, for 18 months. Project management means Project Delivery Foundations, Agile Practitioner Track, and Advanced Project Leadership. IT means Cloud Fundamentals, IT Service Management Essentials, and Network & Security Basics. You do not mix tracks inside one bundle. Mock exams cover every course in the track you chose. Live Q&A is weekly, on Wednesdays at 19:00 CET. A study planner, a certificate of completion for each course you finish, and instructor feedback on two assignments are included. You pay by card, in USD. VAT is shown at checkout. The refund rule is the same as on the other plans: within 14 days, if you have watched less than 20 percent. Lucía Ferrer, who moved from operations coordinator to project coordinator, took the project-management bundle. That story is one account, not a result attached to the price.',
	'faq_q3' => 'How do I pay?',
	'faq_g3' => 'Buying',
	'faq_a3' => 'You pay at checkout by card. Prices are in USD. A single course is charged at that course\'s list price. The pathway bundle is charged at $429. All-access is charged at $690 for all six courses and 24 months of access. VAT is shown at checkout, not as a figure on this page. All-access includes weekly live Q&A, a mock exam for every course, a study planner, a certificate of completion, and instructor feedback on two assignments. When the payment is complete, the course or courses appear in My courses. If you need the charge checked, write to support@shikaku-academy.example during support hours and name the course. The hours are Monday to Friday, 08:00 to 18:00 CET, and Saturday, 09:00 to 13:00 CET. The academy does not describe another way to pay on this site. The step in the process is simply: pay at checkout by card.',
	'faq_q4' => 'Do I have to study at fixed times?',
	'faq_g4' => 'Learning',
	'faq_a4' => 'No. Step 03 is to learn in the lesson player at your pace. The lessons are recordings. Project Delivery Foundations is 18 hours, Agile Practitioner Track is 15 hours, Advanced Project Leadership is 26 hours, Cloud Fundamentals is 16 hours, IT Service Management Essentials is 20 hours, and Network & Security Basics is 22 hours. Those hours are the length of the recordings, not appointments in a week. You open the numbered list when you can, and you stop when you need to, inside your access period. The only fixed time on the calendar is live Q&A, on Wednesdays at 19:00 CET. A single course includes that session monthly. A pathway bundle or all-access includes it weekly. The lessons do not depend on attending Q&A. The player remains available throughout the access you paid for, whether or not you join the Wednesday session.',
	'faq_q5' => 'What is the mock exam?',
	'faq_g5' => 'Learning',
	'faq_a5' => 'Each course has a mock exam. On a single course you receive one. On a pathway bundle you receive the mock exam for each course in the track. On all-access you receive the mock exam for all six courses. You take it after the lessons, as step 04, and then you download the certificate of completion. The exam is part of finishing the academy\'s course. It is not an external certification test, and Shikaku Academy does not name an outside examining body. The certificate says you completed this course. It does not say you passed someone else\'s exam. The academy does not publish a pass rate for the mock exam. Use it as a check on the lessons you have just taken. Instructor feedback on two assignments is a separate item, included only on the pathway bundle and on all-access, not on a single course.',
	'faq_q6' => 'When is live Q&A, and how often can I join?',
	'faq_g6' => 'Learning',
	'faq_a6' => 'Live Q&A is on Wednesdays at 19:00 CET. How often you join depends on the plan you bought, not on which pathway the course belongs to. A single course includes live Q&A monthly. A pathway bundle includes it weekly. All-access includes it weekly. The session is for questions about the courses. It is not a second lecture that replaces the lesson player. If your place is monthly, you still study in other weeks. The recordings do not wait for Wednesday. Learner support stays available by email on the published hours even in a week when you do not join Q&A. Those hours are Monday to Friday, 08:00 to 18:00 CET, and Saturday, 09:00 to 13:00 CET. Priya Raman leads the desk and can pass a teaching question to Tomasz Wierzbicki, Amara Osei, Rafael Quintero, Ingrid Solberg, or Daniel Mwangi.',
	'faq_q7' => 'How long does access last?',
	'faq_g7' => 'Access',
	'faq_a7' => 'Access follows the plan, not the length of the recordings. A single course includes 12 months. A pathway bundle includes 18 months. All-access includes 24 months. During that period you may open the lesson player and move through the numbered lessons at your pace. The study planner, included on every plan, shows the lessons ahead. It does not set a weekly quota. This page states those three periods and no other access length. If you are unsure which period you bought, write to support@shikaku-academy.example and name the course. The certificate of completion, once you have downloaded it after the mock exam, is your record that you finished. The access period is how long the lessons stay open in My courses. Recorded hours are much shorter than these periods: the courses run from 15 hours to 26 hours.',
	'faq_q8' => 'When can I reach learner support?',
	'faq_g8' => 'Access',
	'faq_a8' => 'Learner support is open Monday to Friday from 08:00 to 18:00 CET, and Saturday from 09:00 to 13:00 CET. The email is support@shikaku-academy.example. Priya Raman leads the desk. The support office is at Kade 14, 3072 Rotterdam, Netherlands, which is also the recording studio. You can use the form on the Support page or send email. Include the course name so the note can reach the right instructor if it is a teaching question. Tomasz Wierzbicki teaches courses 01 and 03. Amara Osei teaches course 02. Rafael Quintero teaches course 04. Ingrid Solberg teaches course 05. Daniel Mwangi teaches course 06. A teaching point can also wait for live Q&A on Wednesday at 19:00 CET, at the frequency your plan includes. Payment questions, access questions, and refund requests belong with Priya\'s desk rather than with the Wednesday session.',
	'faq_q9' => 'Do I need to come to Rotterdam?',
	'faq_g9' => 'Access',
	'faq_a9' => 'No. Shikaku Academy is fully online. Kade 14, 3072 Rotterdam, Netherlands is the recording studio and the support office, not a classroom you must attend. Lessons are watched in the lesson player. You pay by card at checkout. Live Q&A is on Wednesdays at 19:00 CET, at the frequency your plan includes, and you join it from where you already are. You can complete a single course, a pathway of three courses, or all six courses without visiting the office. The team of seven is based at that address: Helena Marsh, the instructors who record the courses, and Priya Raman on learner support. The academy was founded in 2017. If you write by email, you reach the desk during the published support hours. Nothing in the four-step process asks you to book travel.',
	'faq_q10' => 'What certificate will I receive?',
	'faq_g10' => 'Certificates',
	'faq_a10' => 'You receive a certificate of completion from Shikaku Academy after you take the mock exam for that course. Every plan includes this certificate: the single course, the pathway bundle, and all-access. It is the academy\'s record that you completed the course you bought here. You download it yourself. Step 04 is that pair of actions: take the mock exam, then download the certificate. If your plan covers more than one course, you download a certificate of completion for each course you finish. The document is not described as an external credential. Helena Marsh, founder and director of studies, keeps that limit on purpose. The courses prepare you for widely recognised project-management and IT credentials. The file you download does not stand in for those credentials. A story on this site never treats the certificate as a salary or as a pass rate.',
	'faq_q11' => 'Does this certificate replace an external credential?',
	'faq_g11' => 'Certificates',
	'faq_a11' => 'No. The courses prepare you for widely recognised project-management and IT credentials. Shikaku Academy does not award those credentials, and it does not use their names or marks. The document you download is a certificate of completion for the course you took here. People who need an outside credential still follow that credential\'s own exam and that body\'s own rules. The academy has no pass rate to show you, because it does not publish one. Use the lessons, the study planner, and the mock exam as preparation. Use the certificate of completion as a record of what you finished here, and nothing further. That limit is the same on a $149 course and on all-access at $690. Buying a longer plan adds courses, months of access, weekly Q&A, and feedback on two assignments. It does not add an outside credential.',
	'faq_q12' => 'Do you publish a pass rate?',
	'faq_g12' => 'Certificates',
	'faq_a12' => 'No. Shikaku Academy does not publish a pass rate for its mock exams or for any outside exam. It also does not publish salary figures, awards, or the names of certification bodies. The three student stories name a role before, a role after, and the course that person took. Lucía Ferrer moved from operations coordinator to project coordinator and took the project-management bundle. Jonas Becker moved from help-desk analyst to service desk lead and took IT Service Management Essentials. Noor Haddad was returning to work, is now a cloud support associate, and took Cloud Fundamentals. Those accounts are not a statistic. The facts that are published, and that stay the same on every page, are the lesson counts, the hours, the USD prices, the access periods of 12, 18, and 24 months, the Wednesday Q&A time, and the support hours.',
	'my_courses_title' => 'My courses',
	'my_courses_intro' => 'My courses lists the courses attached to your purchase. Open one to continue in the lesson player, inside the access period for your plan.',
	'my_courses_h1' => 'The list after you pay',
	'my_courses_b1' => 'My courses is the list of courses attached to the purchase you made at checkout. Log in, and the courses you paid for are there. Open one to return to the lesson player and the numbered lesson list. If you bought a single course, you will see that one title. If you bought the project-management pathway bundle, you will see Project Delivery Foundations, Agile Practitioner Track, and Advanced Project Leadership. If you bought the IT bundle, you will see Cloud Fundamentals, IT Service Management Essentials, and Network & Security Basics. If you bought all-access, you will see all six. A progress marker on each course shows how far you have moved through its lessons. It is not a grade. If the list is empty, the payment has not been attached to this login yet. Write to support@shikaku-academy.example and name the course. The desk is open Monday to Friday from 08:00 to 18:00 CET and Saturday from 09:00 to 13:00 CET.',
	'my_courses_h2' => 'How long the courses stay open',
	'my_courses_b2' => 'Access follows the plan you paid for, and the list follows that period. A single course stays open for 12 months and includes one mock exam, live Q&A monthly, a study planner, and a certificate of completion. It does not include instructor feedback on two assignments. A pathway bundle stays open for 18 months and includes the three courses of the track you chose, mock exams for those courses, live Q&A weekly, the study planner, the certificate, and feedback on two assignments. All-access stays open for 24 months and includes all six courses on those same weekly terms. Live Q&A itself is on Wednesdays at 19:00 CET. When you have taken the mock exam for a course, download the certificate of completion from that course. The certificate is Shikaku Academy\'s, not an outside credential. Prices remain the ones you paid: from $149, or $429, or $690, in USD. A refund, if you still need one, is within 14 days if you have watched less than 20 percent.',
